# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# ...but never for anything this repository reads back as source, which is all of it.
# core.autocrlf is true on the machine this is developed on, so `* text=auto` alone means
# the working tree is LF while a fresh checkout is CRLF - and the damage lands on whoever
# clones next, not on whoever committed.
#
# src/countdown.sh is the case with teeth. /bin/sh cannot parse a CRLF script at all: the
# trailing \r joins the end of every line to the next token, so `set --` fails, the script
# exits 2 having printed nothing, and startCountdownWindow sees a nonzero exit carrying
# neither CHUTDOWN:NOW nor CHUTDOWN:CANCEL - which the three-outcome protocol reads as "the
# window never appeared". It fails safe (the machine stays on, the gear stays armed), but
# every Linux install loses the desktop countdown and wastes its first armed run, and
# `vsce package` reads the working copy, so the broken one is what ships.
#
# The .js half is the trap this repository has already hit once: test/smoke.js regexes over
# src/*.js with \n, and a checkout that flipped the line endings failed five tests that
# looked nothing like a line-ending problem.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
